              <h2>Why Khan Academy Kids &amp; PBS Kids Are Essential (And Great Ways to Complement Them)</h2>
              <p>
                Both <a href="https://learn.khanacademy.org/khan-academy-kids/" target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer">Khan Academy Kids</a> and <a
                  href="https://pbskids.org/apps/pbs-kids-games.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PBS Kids
                  Games</a> are non-profit, 100% free, and completely free of commercial advertisements. For early
                phonics, counting, and familiar television characters, they are unbeatable.
              </p>
              <p>
                Many families also pair Khan Academy Kids and PBS Kids with <strong>offline, open-ended companion
                  apps</strong> that add three wonderful benefits:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>100% Offline Travel Play (Flights &amp; Road Trips):</strong> When you are boarding a long
                  flight or travelling internationally without Wi-Fi, having apps that store all their content locally
                  on your device ensures everything loads instantly in Airplane Mode anywhere in the world.</li>
                <li><strong>Open-Ended, Unscored Exploration:</strong> Alongside guided phonics and math lessons,
                  children love having open-ended Montessori and science sandboxes where there are no quizzes or
                  instructions, allowing them to explore freely at their own pace after school.</li>
                <li><strong>Instant Play Without Accounts:</strong> Apps that launch straight into discovery without
                  requiring an email login or profile setup are wonderfully convenient on shared family tablets.</li>
              </ul>

