              <h2>The 6 Best Alternatives &amp; Companions</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> Best 100% Offline Montessori
                      Nature Companion</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-wifi"></i> 100% Offline Worldwide</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-user-slash"></i> No Account Required</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> One-Time Purchase</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  While Khan Academy Kids excels at structured reading and math exercises, <strong><a
                      href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong> is built for the other half of a child's
                  intellect: <strong>pure, unhurried curiosity about the natural world</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Designed for children ages 4–10, Kidamame Discovery features <strong>zero quizzes, zero instructions,
                    and zero right-or-wrong answers</strong>. Instead, children explore 6 richly illustrated ecosystems
                  (from the Amazon Rainforest and the African Savannah to the Arctic and the Alps), interacting with
                  over 120 animals, plants, and natural phenomena and unlocking <strong>~400 fascinating science
                    facts</strong>.
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Works Worldwide &amp; 100% Offline:</strong> Kidamame Discovery works anywhere on Earth
                    in Airplane Mode and supports 6 languages (English, Italian, French, German, Spanish, and
                    Portuguese).</li>
                  <li><strong>Zero Registration:</strong> Open the app and play immediately. No email sign-ups, no
                    passwords, and no data collection.</li>
                  <li><strong>Try Free, Unlock Once:</strong> Try the app for free and unlock the full world forever
                    with a single one-time purchase.</li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
              </div>

              <!-- 2. TINYBOP -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best for Open-Ended Science Inquiry</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">2. Tinybop's Explorer's Library</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Standalone App Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-flask"></i> 100% Offline Science</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If your child loves PBS shows like <em>Sid the Science Kid</em>, <em>Elinor Wonders Why</em>, or
                  <em>Wild Kratts</em>, <a href="https://tinybop.com/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Tinybop</a>'s standalone apps (<em>The Human Body</em>, <em>Space</em>,
                  <em>Weather</em>, <em>Plants</em>, and <em>Mammals</em>) are an extraordinary next step. Each app works
                  completely offline and lets children test scientific hypotheses by touching and experimenting directly
                  with working models.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Rather than quizzing children, Tinybop trusts their natural
                  curiosity. Kids can watch how a human heart pumps faster when running, spin through the solar system,
                  or create a thunderstorm from scratch, supported by optional text labels in dozens of languages.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 3. DRAGONBOX NUMBERS -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Montessori-Style Math Discovery</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">3. DragonBox Numbers &amp; Big Numbers</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–9</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-calculator"></i> Visual Math (No Drills)</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Instead of multiple-choice math quizzes, <a href="https://dragonbox.com/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">DragonBox Numbers</a> turns numbers into colorful, expressive rods called
                  "Nooms" (inspired by Montessori and Cuisenaire rods) that kids can stack, slice, and combine to
                  intuitively grasp addition, subtraction, and number relationships.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> For older children ages 6–9, its sequel <em>DragonBox Big
                    Numbers</em> seamlessly teaches multi-digit addition, subtraction, carrying, and place value up to
                  the hundred-thousands through a calm resource-gathering world. Both apps build genuine mathematical
                  confidence without ever feeling like a school test.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 4. ENDLESS READER -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Quiz-Free Sight Words &amp; Reading</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">4. Endless Reader &amp; Endless Alphabet (by Originator)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 3–7</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> One-Time Pack Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open"></i> Literacy Without Grading</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Some children freeze up when an app grades their reading answers. Created by the acclaimed studio <a
                    href="https://www.originatorkids.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Originator</a>,
                  <em>Endless Reader</em> and its sibling apps (<em>Endless Alphabet</em>, <em>Endless Numbers</em>, and
                  <em>Endless Wordplay</em>) introduce sight words, vocabulary, and early math through playful puzzles
                  where each letter or number comes alive as your child drags it across the screen.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Once the words are placed into a sentence, the characters act out
                  a charming, humorous animation that shows the meaning of the sentence in context. Because there are no
                  scores, timers, or wrong-answer buzzers, young learners can explore language and numbers with zero
                  pressure.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 5. NIGHTY NIGHT -->
