                    </h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 5–12+ (Family Co-Use)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free (Non-Profit)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-dove"></i> Sound ID &amp; Nature</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Built by Cornell University, <a href="https://www.merlinbirds.org/download/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Merlin Bird ID</a> lets kids and parents hold up a phone on a morning walk
                  and see real-time highlights of which birds are singing in the trees around them. Like Khan Academy
                  Kids and PBS Kids, it is 100% free and non-profit, and it turns screen time into an unforgettable
                  outdoor family ritual.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why it stands out:</strong> Families can download regional bird packs for offline use anywhere
                  in the world, compare calls from the Macaulay Library, and learn to recognize local wildlife by ear.
                </p>
              </div>

